  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Intersection",
    "description": "Intersection is a free game on the Google Play store that is available for Android phones. I made this game over the course of about 1 month using Java and Android Studio. It is my first publicly released game and I hope you give it a try!",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "May 2015 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "Mrs. PacMan Genetic Neural Networks",
    "description": "Mrs. PacMan Genetic Neural Networks is a project that I worked on so I could learn more about Learning and Neural Networks. As a base I am using a Mrs. PacMan clone that was made for an AI competition. The first thing that I did was learn how to program neural networks without using an outside libary. Once I had the neural net done I next had to get it so that I could control Mrs. PacMan with the net. This was an important step because if the inputs into the net wasn't describing the game space well, then the net would have a difficult time solving the game. In order to get the neural net to learn I decided to use a genetic algorithm, the genetic algorithm can only change the weights inside the neural net. At first, finding the fitnesses of all the nets of a genetation took quite a while, so each net now finds it's fitness simultaiously by all running on different threads. Once I got all of these parts working, It took a lot of tweaking the genetic algorithm and of the nets in order to get a good result. In the neural nets I would tweak the number of inputs, number of hidden layers, and number of nodes in each layer. In the genetic algorithm I would change what kind of gene crossover I would use, at first I was using single point crossover, however this caused premature convergence, so I canged it to uniform corssover, I also would tweak the mutaion rate and the population size. Once I had all of the algorithms done I decided to make a GUI for the program so it was easier to visualize how the populations were growing, to do this I had to learn about JPanels, and that I had to run it in it's own thread so that I could update it while the rest of the program was still running. ",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Sep 2013 - Present"
   }
